safix::bitwarden_item_absent

  × the mapping 'router' is bitwarden-to-safix, so the vault is where its
  │ value comes from,
  │ and the vault holds no item at 'fleet/router'. Nothing was written.
  │ 
  │ safix does not author that item, and this is the one place the asymmetry
  │ shows: a value the operator types into their own vault is theirs to
  │ create,
  │ where a value safix mints is safix's. Create it, and the next run
  │ converges
  │ safix onto it.
  │ 
  │ If safix is the producer after all, the mapping is declared the wrong way
  │ round: mode = "safix-to-bitwarden" makes the vault follow safix.
